---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import BioContactForm from "../../components/BioContactForm.astro";
import ajHeadshot from "../../assets/team/aj-headshot-consistent.jpg";
import danArmy from "../../assets/team/dan-army-transparent.png";
import danCredentials from "../../assets/team/dan-credentials-transparent.png";
import danHeadshot from "../../assets/team/dan-headshot-consistent.jpg";
import dougCredentials from "../../assets/team/doug-credentials-transparent.png";
import dougHeadshot from "../../assets/team/doug-headshot-consistent.jpg";
import janCredentials from "../../assets/team/jan-credentials-transparent.png";
import janHeadshot from "../../assets/team/jan-headshot-consistent.jpg";
import marcHeadshot from "../../assets/team/marc-headshot-consistent.jpg";
import marceloCredentials from "../../assets/team/marcelo-credentials-transparent.png";
import marceloHeadshot from "../../assets/team/marcelo-headshot-consistent.jpg";
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { pageSeo } from "../../seo/registry.mjs";

const bios = {
	"doug-shimp": { name: "Doug Shimp", title: "Senior Agility Instructor", image: dougHeadshot, credentials: [dougCredentials], sections: [["Doug Shimp started as an entrepreneur at a young age, practicing agile before even knowing the term. Leading a business required teamwork, rapid feedback loops, and daily stand-ups. These practices helped ensure projects met stakeholder expectations, delivered on time, and stayed within budget. Through this hands-on experience, Doug discovered the value of the Scrum framework.", "This work represents a foundational chapter of my career, focused on building strong teams through Scrum and systems thinking, principles I continue to apply today in broader technology and business contexts.", "Doug’s career transitioned from being a business owner to pursuing graduate studies in biomolecular chemistry and software development. During this time, he wrote code in C, C++, and Smalltalk. This experience taught him the importance of encapsulation and clean code. Always curious, Doug later turned his focus to the study of methodologies, object modeling, and use cases. Currently, he is exploring the connection between interactive marketing, Innovation Games®, and Scrum practices. Doug believes the key to success, whether in coding, use cases, or innovation games, lies in forming a strong team."], ["Founder", "Today, that same focus on teams, feedback, and learning informs my work applying modern technology, including AI, to real business problems.\nAs the founder of 3Back, Doug has worked with companies of all sizes, from Fortune 50 giants to small start-ups. Teams and leadership alike benefit from his deep Scrum knowledge. Doug excels at asking the right questions to help organizations improve their product development processes through Scrum. His engaging, hands-on training sessions create momentum, inspiring teams to apply Scrum to real-world challenges. Whether training rookies or seasoned veterans, Doug equips learners to implement Scrum effectively."], ["Author", "Doug is the co-author of Exploring Scrum: The Fundamentals, a book that shares his lifelong experience and knowledge in an easy-to-read format. Beyond his books, Doug developed the Scrum Leadership Series. This series offers a comprehensive set of courses aimed at improving leadership in Scrum teams. Additionally, Doug created Get to Done®, a team-friendly software tool. This “cards-on-wall” and online tool helps Scrum teams foster productive communication patterns. Get to Done® directly reflects the patterns explored in the Scrum classroom."], ["Life Beyond Work", "Outside of work, Doug values time with family and friends and staying connected to the community he lives in. He enjoys cycling and swimming along Lake Michigan, attending local events and gatherings, and being present in the relationships and places that matter most to him."]]},
	"dan-rawsthorne": { name: "Dan Rawsthorne", title: "Chief Scientist and Senior Agility Instructor", image: danHeadshot, credentials: [danCredentials, danArmy], sections: [["From Military Intelligence to Scrum intelligence, Dan Rawsthorne has been applying agile for a significant period. He began his agile journey with the military, one of the largest long-term users of agile principles. As a U.S. Army officer, Dan was tasked with applying artificial intelligence to computer security and developing advanced battlefield management systems. These systems were used during the Persian Gulf War to improve decision-making on the battlefield. Now retired from the military, Dan has shifted his focus to the training room. He has been teaching and coaching thousands of learners and organizations across the globe.", "Dan is a recognized pioneer in the Scrum community, with years of experience working in the trenches as an expert in agility, use cases, and object-oriented technologies. He has held nearly every conceivable role in software development, from Coder to Systems Analyst, Business Analyst, Architect, Team Leader, Project Manager, QA Director, and even Engineering Director. His sharp skills and extensive experience with a variety of agile tools and techniques—such as RUP, XP, Scrum, UML, and Get to Done®—have made him a well-rounded and highly respected expert in the field."], ["Accomplished Author – Dan", "In addition to his practical expertise, Dan has also made significant contributions to the Scrum knowledge base. He co-authored Exploring Scrum: The Fundamentals with Doug Shimp, a comprehensive 300-page reference book. This book is designed to help professionals navigate common impediments, improve processes, and master the practical applications of Scrum. Exploring Scrum represents the culmination of Dan’s work so far, but he isn’t stopping there. He is currently working on a new book focused on Agile Project Management, which promises to further expand his contributions to the agile community."], ["", "At 3Back, Dan serves as a transformation agent, helping organizations improve through the application of agile methodologies like Scrum. His PhD in Mathematics enables him to identify and address underlying problems in systems, while his military background gives him a deep understanding of the importance of teamwork and empowerment. Dan firmly believes that meaningful change must occur in small, manageable steps to be effective.\n\nWhen he’s not transforming organizations, Dan brings his focus and determination to the bowling alley. A perfect 300 game is often within his reach, and if you take a peek inside his extra bags, you might find not one, but several bowling balls, ready for action!"]]},
	"marcelo-lopez-jr": { name: "Marcelo Lopez Jr.", title: "Senior Agility Instructor", image: marceloHeadshot, credentials: [marceloCredentials], sections: [["Marcelo tried to fix his father’s shortwave radio when he was 9 years old. To their surprise, and relief, it worked. This was the first milestone in an extensive product development career.", "With his thirty years of coding experience in operating systems for bio-medical device instrumentation and high-throughput financial transaction processing systems, to say Marcelo understands the world of engineers, is an understatement. However, having experienced ‘Command and Control’ structures in these heavily regulated industries, he felt there was a better way to get things done; something that could spur innovation, deliver higher quality solutions and yet adapt to ever changing business demands. The solution? Scrum.", "Marcelo understands what it takes for Scrum to thrive within the constraints of regulations, deadlines and budgets. As an experienced ScrumMaster and uber Product Owner in a bio-medical instrument organization, Marcelo appreciated the constraints of Scrum with stringent Class 2 and Class 3 device regulations as well as 510K submittal requirements. As a Lead Developer for the User Experience for many years, Marcelo recognized the challenges of development in a clinical setting. These strict product development settings, and many more like them, are prime for the application of the Scrum framework. Marcelo has the knowledge and skills to balance the voice of the Customer, the needs of the business and bring high quality products to market."], ["Near Shore with Marcelo Lopez Jr.", "With the growing trend of nearshore development, Marcelo’s ability to deliver the Scrum message in both Spanish and English are pure gold. When Scrum.org needed the Scrum Guide to go further into the world, Marcelo jumped on the chance to deliver the Spanish translation, the first non-English version of the Scrum Guide to be published. Marcelo went on to translate “Scrum in a Nutshell” into Spanish, “Scrum en Breve”. Next up for Marcelo’s translation skills? A Spanish language version of the “Scrum Study Guide”.\n\nWhen not thinking about building better products, Marcelo applies his agile thinking to navigating his bike around South Florida. An avid photographer, you might find him taking pictures at various botanical gardens or in the Everglades. It’s also not uncommon to see the sign “Gone Fishin’” at his place; not surprising, given his proximity to the Florida Keys.\n\nHablas Scrum? Llegamos a “Hecho”, juntos! (Do you speak Scrum? We’ll get to “Done”, together!)\n\nIn addition to being a Certified ScrumMaster (CSM) and Certified Scrum Product Owner (CSPO), Marcelo also holds the more rigorous designation of Certified Scrum Professional (CSP) with the Scrum Alliance. Marcelo is also an Accredited Kanban Trainer (AKT) through Lean Kanban University."]]},
	"aj-biddles": { name: "AJ Biddles", title: "Senior Agility Instructor", image: ajHeadshot, credentials: [], sections: [["Code drips from AJ Biddles’ fingers. And not just any code. Clean, quality code. AJ is hard-wired for software development with his dad writing code for as long as AJ can remember. Developing code alongside his dad, there was overriding conviction of testability. Their mantra was: Write clean code and test first. Dad worked on back-end stuff while AJ worked on the middle tier. Sitting side by side, they kicked out more clean code and great stuff than most teams with twice the manpower.", "For AJ, clean code is about pride in craftsmanship. Coding is like painting the Mona Lisa; it engages the left and right sides of your brain. It’s creative, it’s a science, and it’s an art. Code must be easy to read and well written. Only then is code easy to maintain.", "AJ’s fondest memory was working on a remote TeamLet development project. Sitting within inches of each other, feedback and requirements flew fast and furious. Code would be written and tested within minutes. A quick game of foosball over lunch and they were back cranking out code ’til the wee hours of the morning.", "As a key Developer for Get to Done®, AJ appreciates the approach. Get to Done® is an agile company doing software, rather than a software company doing agile. The Get to Done® tool coaches the correct Scrum team behavior and that’s the difference. Most tools dictate the behavior, but good Scrum behavior dictates the Get to Done® tool development.", "Approaching Scrum training from the developer point of view, AJ always has been and always will be a geek. When he’s not coding for fun, AJ is running the scoreboard for his daughter’s games or riding the waves on his jet-ski in the bright, blue waters of Florida.", "In addition to holding Scrum Alliance certifications for Certified ScrumMaster (CSM) and Certified Scrum Product Owner (CSPO), AJ also holds the more rigorous certification for Certified Scrum Professional (CSP)."]]},
	"jan-beaver": { name: "Jan Beaver", title: "Senior Agility Instructor", image: janHeadshot, credentials: [janCredentials], sections: [["Jan Beaver, a Ph.D. educator, brings over 25 years of experience in the software industry. His background spans development, QA, management, and technical writing. As a skilled agile coach and trainer, Jan excels in applying Scrum, agile, and lean principles to help teams improve. He specializes in guiding teams to become effective, productive, and self-sustaining. He also works at the enterprise level, driving agile transformations to ensure success.", "With a wealth of experience in the software field, Jan’s resume covers roles in management, development, QA, and technical writing. His introduction to Scrum was a transformative experience, reinforcing his belief that teamwork is crucial for product development. Jan emphasizes that when the focus is on building strong teams, there are no limits to what an organization can achieve. For him, a great team is defined by shared goals, a common vision, and a high level of collaboration.", "Jan has worked with companies of all sizes in various industries, including telecommunications, medical, insurance, financial services, media, utilities, education, and smart-grid energy. His expertise in Scrum, Agile, and Lean practices enables him to lead teams toward becoming more effective and sustainable. He also believes organizational leadership is key to building trust, accountability, and effectiveness at every level.", "Eager to share his insights, Jan authored *The Agile Team Handbook*. This practical guide is designed to help teams and organizations apply Agile values and Scrum principles to succeed in today’s fast-paced business world. The book offers hands-on strategies for building sustainable, productive teams and creating outstanding work environments.", "When not sharing his expertise in Scrum, Jan enjoys bicycling, fly fishing, and camping. His favorite spot to camp? The beautiful Colorado Rockies, which just happen to be his backyard."]]},
	"marc-applebaum": { name: "Marc Applebaum", title: "Senior Agility Instructor", image: marcHeadshot, credentials: [], sections: [["Marc Applebaum brings a unique combination of executive coaching expertise and psychological research experience. With over 15 years of experience, he has coached business founders, senior managers, and teams. His coaching helps clients navigate leadership, communication, and change management with confidence. Marc’s hands-on approach allows him to work closely with leaders to identify obstacles to success. He empowers clients to address challenges and become more effective and creative.", "His coaching spans industries in the San Francisco Bay Area and Silicon Valley. Marc has worked with biotech, ecommerce, advertising, design, and health & wellness companies. His clients include startups and established businesses. Despite industry differences, his clients share a desire for greater personal and team effectiveness. They seek improved decision-making clarity and confidence in high-demand environments. Marc helps leaders find ease and adaptability amid constant activity.", "In addition to his coaching, Marc is a respected academic. He teaches at Saybrook University in San Francisco as a faculty member in Psychology and Interdisciplinary Inquiry. He also contributes to research and serves on the Editorial Board of several psychology journals. Currently, Marc is conducting a study on Silicon Valley executives. His research explores leadership challenges and how executives adapt.", "Marc’s blend of coaching expertise and academic knowledge makes him an invaluable resource for leaders. He helps them thrive both personally and professionally, enabling long-term success."]]},
};

export function getStaticPaths() {
	return ["doug-shimp", "dan-rawsthorne", "marcelo-lopez-jr", "aj-biddles", "jan-beaver", "marc-applebaum"].map((slug) => ({ params: { slug } }));
}

const slug = Astro.params.slug;
const bio = bios[slug as keyof typeof bios];
---

<SiteLayout metadata={pageSeo[`/team/${slug}`]}>
	<main id="main" class="bio-page">
		<section class="bio-hero"><div class="shell bio-hero-inner"><p class="eyebrow">The Team</p><h1>{bio.name}</h1><p class="title">{bio.title}</p><a class="contact-trigger" href="#bio-contact">Contact {bio.name.split(" ")[0]}</a></div></section>
		<section class="section"><div class="shell bio-grid"><Image class="headshot" src={bio.image} alt={`Portrait of ${bio.name}`} widths={[480, 720]} sizes="(max-width: 820px) calc(100vw - 48px), 38vw" /><div class="bio-copy">{bio.sections.map(([heading, content]) => <section>{heading && <h2>{heading}</h2>}{content.split("\n\n").map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}</section>)}</div></div></section>
		{bio.credentials.length > 0 && <section class="credentials"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Credentials</p><div class="credential-grid">{bio.credentials.map((credential) => <Image src={credential} alt={`${bio.name} credential plate`} layout="constrained" />)}</div></div></section>}
		<BioContactForm instructorName={bio.name} instructorSlug={slug!} />
	</main>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
	.bio-hero { padding: 110px 0 70px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
	.eyebrow { margin-bottom: 14px; color: var(--amber-text); font-size: var(--type-caption); font-weight: var(--font-weight-heavy); letter-spacing: var(--tracking-caption); text-transform: uppercase; }
	.bio-hero h1 { margin-bottom: 16px; }
	.title { max-width: 38ch; margin: 0; color: var(--slate); font-size: var(--type-lead); font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold); }
	.contact-trigger { display: inline-block; margin-top: 24px; color: var(--charcoal); font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold); text-underline-offset: 5px; }
	.contact-trigger:hover { color: var(--amber-text); }
	.bio-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(260px, .72fr) minmax(0, 1.28fr); align-items: start; gap: clamp(44px, 8vw, 124px); }
	.headshot { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto !important; max-width: 100%; aspect-ratio: auto !important; object-fit: contain; border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--reading); }
	.bio-copy { max-width: 72ch; }
	.bio-copy section + section { margin-top: 46px; }
	.bio-copy h2 { margin-bottom: 18px; font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.4rem); }
	.bio-copy p { margin-bottom: 24px; font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.7; white-space: pre-line; }
	.credentials { padding: 80px 0 110px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
	.credential-grid { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 30px; }
	.credential-grid :global(img) { display: block; max-width: min(100%, 460px); height: auto; }
	@media (max-width: 820px) { .bio-hero { padding: 82px 0 52px; } .bio-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .headshot { max-width: 520px; } .credentials { padding: 66px 0 78px; } }
</style>
